  "report": "Implementation review passed; operator acceptance remains separate.\n\nRESULT: **accepted for the PYTHON-SUBMODULE-IMPORT-1 slice; not a release approval.** I found no blocking defect in the 16-path uncommitted candidate at `HEAD a715462044a1ca58b1c620ff8ade476241bfd67d`. The ratified release gate remains: TEST-EDGE-SCOPE-1B must partition the other IMPORTS consumers before release.\n\n**Verification basis.** OBSERVED `git status`, the complete candidate diff, `git diff --check` (exit 0), the relevant source and tests, and the builder’s evidence files under `.agent-manager/slices/PYTHON-SUBMODULE-IMPORT-1/evidence-2/`. EXECUTED independently: resolver 138 passed; orchestrator 21; storage importer 5; agent explain 20; rgr explain 51; repo-index Python integration 5; the affected daemon test 1; `cargo fmt --check` exit 0. I relied on **BUILDER-EXECUTED** evidence for the whole daemon library suite, clippy, isolated-store comparisons, refresh parity, stale-toolchain CLI proof, and registry/cleanup proof. My attempted whole-daemon run did not yield a final exit status, so I do not count it as independently reproduced.\n\n| Check | Assessment and basis |\n|---|---|\n| PSI-C01 | **Accepted.** EXECUTED resolver and orchestrator suites; OBSERVED version bump and copied-signal read. Remaining source assertions: BUILDER-EXECUTED. |\n| PSI-C02 | **Accepted.** EXECUTED the affected storage, agent, rgr, integration and daemon tests; whole daemon suite and unchanged-file guard: BUILDER-EXECUTED. |\n| PSI-C03 | **Accepted.** EXECUTED formatting check; clippy: BUILDER-EXECUTED. |\n| PSI-C04 | **Accepted on BUILDER-EXECUTED store oracle**, with OBSERVED source lines and captures. Django: 1,440 imports become inferred; module pairs 2,451→2,084; unresolved rows unchanged. FRAKTAG row identity was not independently rerun. |\n| PSI-C06 | **Accepted on BUILDER-EXECUTED parity oracle:** 3,019 file versions, 3,015 signal rows, 81,601 IMPORTS+CALLS edges and 90,640 unresolved rows match across full index and no-change refresh. |\n| PSI-C07 | **Accepted on BUILDER-EXECUTED isolated CLI proof:** stale `1.0.0→1.1.0` line, unchanged check verdict, and current after-store. |\n| PSI-C05 | **Accepted.** OBSERVED current 16-path status and clean diff check; registry digest, process and temporary-root cleanup: BUILDER-EXECUTED. |\n\n**Independent witness inspection.** OBSERVED Django source contains `django/core/handlers/wsgi.py:5` `from django.core.handlers import base`, used by `class WSGIHandler(base.BaseHandler):` at line 113. The candidate capture shows `Referenced by (1 files, +2 inferred — investigate)` with `asgi.py` and `wsgi.py` naming `django/core/handlers/__init__.py` as alternate; the `imports wsgi.py` capture shows `django/core/handlers/base.py  depth=1  inferred`. OBSERVED `django/shortcuts.py:13` `from django.template import loader`, and the residual `django/db/models/__init__.py:2` `from django.db.models import signals`. The before/after bindings and corpus totals rely on PSI-C04’s builder-executed store oracle, not on source inspection alone.\n\n**Obligation assessments — accepted relative to this allocation, not claims that the catalog Ls are globally complete:**\n\n- Implemented: `RG-REQ-006-L04`.\n- Changed, with the allocated limits: `RG-REQ-002-L11` **partial**; `RG-REQ-001-L06` toolchain signal; `RG-REQ-001-L09` refresh-signal parity, **not** its separate reindex-twice proof.\n- Preserved within the checked scope: `RG-REQ-006-L01`, `L02`, `L03`, `L05`, `L06`, `L07`, `L08`, `L09`, `L10`, `L11`, `L12`, `L13`; `RG-REQ-002-L01`, `L02`, `L03`, `L04`, `L05`, `L06`, `L07`, `L08`, `L09`, `L10`; `RG-REQ-011-L06`; `P-PSI-01`, `P-PSI-02`, `P-PSI-03`. Corpus-scale preservation and isolation assessments rely on the identified builder-executed checks.\n- OBSERVED allocation metadata enumerates **30** distinct IDs (27 L and 3 P), not the task directive’s stated “28”; all 30 are assessed above.\n\n**Changed-path assessments.** Accepted: `indexer/src/resolver.rs` (gated inference and candidate carrier); `indexer/src/orchestrator.rs` (version and refresh signals); `repo-index/tests/integration.rs` and its four new `package-import` fixture files (three-target vertical test); `storage/src/agent_impl.rs` and `storage/tests/agent_impl.rs` (strict certainty read and alternate lookup); `agent/src/storage_port.rs`, `agent/src/dto/signal.rs`, `agent/src/explain/mod.rs`, `agent/tests/explain_symbol.rs` (boundary data and certain/inferred partition); `rgr/src/presentation/explain_sections.rs`, `rgr/src/presentation/explain.rs` (validated reader wording and overflow cases); `daemon-runtime/src/explain_serve_tests/mod.rs` (the authorized one-token canonical-resolution fixture correction). OBSERVED `repo-index/src/compose.rs` is allocated but unchanged. No changed path is outside the approved candidate set.\n\nUnder the hood, the resolver consults indexed package-init facts before the existing import ladder, records the submodule edge as **inferred** with the init as alternate, and withholds that edge from certain module-edge derivation. Refresh now reads copied-forward signals before resolution, so unchanged init bindings remain visible. Storage rejects unknown certainty values; `explain` counts a file as certain only when it has a static or dynamic import and presents inferred-only importers for investigation. This serves the VISION’s first-sixty-seconds discovery goal without promoting a Python runtime-dependent choice to an extracted fact.\n\n**Findings:** none. **Decisions required:** none. **Residual:** other IMPORTS readers can still present these new inferred edges without this partition; the documented TEST-EDGE-SCOPE-1B release gate is therefore material, not waived."
